 expression of N- or E-cadherin. <source>Development.</source> <volume>128</volume>:<fpage>459</fpage>&#x02013;469.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11171330</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Navarro, P., L. Ruco, and E. Dejana. <year>1998</year>. Differential localization of VE- and N-cadherins in human endothelial cells: VE-cadherin competes with N-cadherin for junctional localization. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>140</volume>:<fpage>1475</fpage>&#x02013;1484.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9508779</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Paik, J.H., A. Skoura, S.S. Chae, A.E. Cowan, D.K. Han, R.L. Proia, and T. Hla. <year>2004</year>. Sphingosine 1-phosphate receptor regulation of N-cadherin mediates vascular stabilization. <source>Genes Dev.</source> <volume>18</volume>:<fpage>2392</fpage>&#x02013;2403.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15371328</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Serini, G., D. Valdembri, S. Zanivan, G. Morterra, C. Burkhardt, F. Caccavari, L. Zammataro, L. Primo, L. Tamagnone, M. Logan, et al. <year>2003</year>. Class 3 semaphorins control vascular morphogenesis by inhibiting integrin function. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>424</volume>:<fpage>391</fpage>&#x02013;397.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12879061</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Wheelock, M.J., and K.R. Johnson. <year>2003</year>. Cadherins as modulators of cellular phenotype. <source>Annu. Rev. Cell Dev. Biol.</source> <volume>19</volume>:<fpage>207</fpage>&#x02013;235.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14570569</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Xiao, K., D.F. Allison, K.M. Buckley, M.D. Kottke, P.A. Vincent, V. Faundez, and A.P. Kowalczyk. <year>2003</year>. Cellular levels of p120 catenin function as a set point for cadherin expression levels in microvascular endothelial cells. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>163</volume>:<fpage>535</fpage>&#x02013;545.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14610056</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Xu, X., W.E. Li, G.Y. Huang, R. Meyer, T. Chen, Y. Luo, M.P. Thomas, G.L. Radice, and C.W. Lo. <year>2001</year>. Modulation of mouse neural crest cell motility by N-cadherin and connexin 43 gap junctions. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>154</volume>:<fpage>217</fpage>&#x02013;230.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11449002</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Yancopoulos, G.D., S. Davis, N.W. Gale, J.S. Rudge, S.J. Wiegand, and J. Holash. <year>2000</year>. Vascular-specific growth factors and blood vessel formation. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>407</volume>:<fpage>242</fpage>&#x02013;248.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11001067</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>